            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 29-year-old woman presented with peracute pain in the right lower quadrant of her abdomen, which at diagnostic laparoscopy appeared to be related to hematoperitoneum caused by bleeding ofa corpus rubrum.</AbstractText>
